# Scope, literal slots and expansion.
#
# GENERATED by tools/gen-sql-scope-cases.py -- do not edit. Every expected
# string is derived, not observed: a scoping case equals the translation of its
# alpha-equivalent control (a binder renamed, an outer `_K` written out), and a
# BUCKET SUM case equals the known-good statement with the body's own
# rendering swapped in. tools/gen-sql-scope-cases.py --check regenerates and
# compares. Each capture case is followed by its control, which must pass
# everywhere; a host that fails only the capture case has a scoping bug.

### name: agg.scope.outer-key-in-inner-list
--- note
A static list's elements are evaluated in the scope the list is written in: `_K` inside the inner list is the OUTER element's key, "1" then "2", and the outer aggregate unrolls twice. The translation used the inner key in both halves and was constantly FALSE where SEL says TRUE. Expected: the outer unroll written out by hand.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{}
--- source
ANY((0,0), ALL((_K, 5), I, I > 1))
--- expect
(((CASE WHEN ('1' REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST('1' AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END > 1) AND (5 > 1)) OR ((CASE WHEN ('2' REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST('2' AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END > 1) AND (5 > 1)))
===

### name: agg.scope.outer-key-in-inner-list-control
--- note
Alpha-equivalent control for agg.scope.outer-key-in-inner-list.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{}
--- source
ALL(("1", 5), I, I > 1) OR ALL(("2", 5), I, I > 1)
--- expect
(((CASE WHEN ('1' REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST('1' AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END > 1) AND (5 > 1)) OR ((CASE WHEN ('2' REGEXP '\\A-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?\\z') THEN CAST('2' AS DECIMAL(65,10)) ELSE NULL END > 1) AND (5 > 1)))
===

### name: agg.scope.element-named-like-inner-binder
--- note
The inner binder A shadows the column A INSIDE the inner body only. The outer element `A` is the column, and the body reads the outer binder I, so the inner body is the outer element compared with 0, twice. Expected: the program with the inner binder renamed.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ALL((A, 1), I, ALL((5, 6), A, I > 0))
--- expect
(((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)) AND ((1 > 0) AND (1 > 0)))
===

### name: agg.scope.element-named-like-inner-binder-control
--- note
Alpha-equivalent control for agg.scope.element-named-like-inner-binder.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ALL((A, 1), I, ALL((5, 6), B, I > 0))
--- expect
(((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)) AND ((1 > 0) AND (1 > 0)))
===

### name: agg.scope.default-binder-nested-static
--- note
Both aggregates use the default binder `_`. The inner list's `_` is the OUTER element; the inner body's `_` is the inner one. It used to be refused as E_SQL_DEPTH ('the evaluator answers E_DEPTH'), which is false: SEL evaluates it. Expected: distinct binder names.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ANY((A, 2), ALL((_, 5), _ > 0))
--- expect
(((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (5 > 0)) OR ((2 > 0) AND (5 > 0)))
===

