{"A": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}, "B": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "b", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
R[1] = A; X = R; SUM(X, _ + 1)
--- expect
(`t`.`a` + 1)
===

### name: plan.helper.rebinds-relation-once
--- note
`ORDERS = ORDERS .> DROP(2)` reads the ORDERS binding once; the later `ORDERS .> TAKE(3)` reads the helper. The pipeline is DROP 2 then TAKE 3 (OFFSET 2 LIMIT 3), not DROP applied twice.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ORDERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "orders", "alias": "o", "fields": {"ID": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ORDERS = ORDERS .> DROP(2); ORDERS .> TAKE(3)
--- plan
pure_sql
--- tables
orders
--- expect
SELECT `o`.* FROM `orders` `o` LIMIT 3 OFFSET 2
===

### name: plan.helper.rebinds-relation-once-control
--- note
The same statement written without the rebinding.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ORDERS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "orders", "alias": "o", "fields": {"ID": {"kind": "column", "table": "o", "column": "id", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- source
ORDERS .> DROP(2) .> TAKE(3)
--- plan
pure_sql
--- tables
orders
--- expect
SELECT `o`.* FROM `orders` `o` LIMIT 3 OFFSET 2
===

### name: agg.join.filtered-source-is-refused
--- note
FILTER yields a list; only ALL, ANY, SUM and COUNT absorb it (docs/internals/sql-translation.md 7.5), so JOIN over one is E_SQL_SHAPE at the FILTER. Every host dropped the FILTER and joined the whole list.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{}
--- source
JOIN(FILTER(("a","b","c"), _ $== "a"), ",")
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:6
===

### name: agg.join.filtered-source-is-refused-constant-false
--- note
Even a predicate that is constantly FALSE: the answer is "", not "a,b,c".
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{}
--- source
JOIN(FILTER(("a","b","c"), FALSE), ",")
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:6
===

### name: agg.filter.absorbed-into-any-control
--- note
Control: the four absorbed shapes still translate.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{}
--- source
ANY(FILTER(("a","b"), _ $== "a"), _ $== "a")
--- expect
(((CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin) AND (CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin)) OR ((CAST('b' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin) AND (CAST('b' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin)))
===

### name: agg.filter.absorbed-into-any-control-control
--- note
Alpha-equivalent control for agg.filter.absorbed-into-any-control.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{}
--- source
ANY(("a","b"), _ $== "a" AND _ $== "a")
--- expect
(((CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin) AND (CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin)) OR ((CAST('b' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin) AND (CAST('b' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin = CAST('a' AS CHAR) COLLATE utf8mb4_nopad_bin)))
===

### name: shape.binder.non-name-binder-is-refused
--- note
A binder position holding an index expression is refused (E_SQL_SHAPE at the index), never a nil dereference.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
BUCKET("x", A[1], "y", 1)
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:14
===

### name: limit.inline-chain-past-the-depth-limit-over-a-column
--- note
250 chained helpers over a column inline to an expression 250 deep: past the evaluator's own MAX_DEPTH (errors.md, E_SQL_DEPTH), so a refusal with that code -- never a host stack overflow (hosts once died: SIGSEGV at 60000, RangeError at 20000).
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
