### name: limit.size.doubling-helper-over-a-column
--- note
19 statements: `X18 > 0` is 2^19+1 = 524 289 nodes once every read of a helper is expanded, over twice MAX_SQL_NODES. Refused with E_SQL_SIZE, quickly: the walk stops at the first node over the limit.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
X0 = N; X1 = X0 + X0; X2 = X1 + X1; X3 = X2 + X2; X4 = X3 + X3; X5 = X4 + X4; X6 = X5 + X5; X7 = X6 + X6; X8 = X7 + X7; X9 = X8 + X8; X10 = X9 + X9; X11 = X10 + X10; X12 = X11 + X11; X13 = X12 + X12; X14 = X13 + X13; X15 = X14 + X14; X16 = X15 + X15; X17 = X16 + X16; X18 = X17 + X17; X18 > 0
--- error
E_SQL_SIZE
===

### name: limit.size.doubling-helper-over-a-constant
--- note
The same over a literal. The count is taken before constant folding hands a subtree to SEL's evaluator, so this is the same refusal and not a slow answer.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{}
--- source
X0 = 1; X1 = X0 + X0; X2 = X1 + X1; X3 = X2 + X2; X4 = X3 + X3; X5 = X4 + X4; X6 = X5 + X5; X7 = X6 + X6; X8 = X7 + X7; X9 = X8 + X8; X10 = X9 + X9; X11 = X10 + X10; X12 = X11 + X11; X13 = X12 + X12; X14 = X13 + X13; X15 = X14 + X14; X16 = X15 + X15; X17 = X16 + X16; X18 = X17 + X17; X18 > 0
--- error
E_SQL_SIZE
===

### name: limit.size.nested-aggregates-over-static-lists
--- note
17 nested `ALL((V,V), W, ...)` levels: two unrolled elements per level, so the innermost body is instantiated 2^16 times and the expression is 2^19-1 nodes.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ALL((A,A), V1, ALL((V1,V1), V2, ALL((V2,V2), V3, ALL((V3,V3), V4, ALL((V4,V4), V5, ALL((V5,V5), V6, ALL((V6,V6), V7, ALL((V7,V7), V8, ALL((V8,V8), V9, ALL((V9,V9), V10, ALL((V10,V10), V11, ALL((V11,V11), V12, ALL((V12,V12), V13, ALL((V13,V13), V14, ALL((V14,V14), V15, ALL((V15,V15), V16, ALL((V16,V16), V17, V17 > 0)))))))))))))))))
--- error
E_SQL_SIZE
===

### name: limit.size.small-doubling-is-accepted
--- note
Control: the same shape at k = 3 (17 nodes) translates.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"N": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "n", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
X0 = N; X1 = X0 + X0; X2 = X1 + X1; X3 = X2 + X2; X3 > 0
--- expect
((((`t`.`n` + `t`.`n`) + (`t`.`n` + `t`.`n`)) + ((`t`.`n` + `t`.`n`) + (`t`.`n` + `t`.`n`))) > 0)
===

### name: limit.size.small-nested-is-accepted
--- note
Control: the nested shape at n = 4 (63 nodes) translates.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"A": {"kind": "column", "table": "t", "column": "a", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
ALL((A,A), V1, ALL((V1,V1), V2, ALL((V2,V2), V3, ALL((V3,V3), V4, V4 > 0))))
--- expect
(((((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)) AND ((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0))) AND (((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)) AND ((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)))) AND ((((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)) AND ((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0))) AND (((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)) AND ((`t`.`a` > 0) AND (`t`.`a` > 0)))))
===

### name: shape.binder.non-name-binder-in-map-statement
--- note
A binder position holding something that is not a name is E_SQL_SHAPE at that expression, in the statement forms too, never a crash or a different code.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items", "alias": "i", "fields": {"DEPT": {"kind": "column", "table": "i", "column": "dept", "type": "TEXT"}, "QTY": {"kind": "column", "table": "i", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> MAP(BUCKET("x", _["DEPT"], "x", _["QTY"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:27
===

### name: shape.binder.non-name-binder-in-bucket-projection-statement
--- note
A binder position holding something that is not a name is E_SQL_SHAPE at that expression, in the statement forms too, never a crash or a different code.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"ITEMS": {"kind": "relation", "from": "items", "alias": "i", "fields": {"DEPT": {"kind": "column", "table": "i", "column": "dept", "type": "TEXT"}, "QTY": {"kind": "column", "table": "i", "column": "qty", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
ITEMS .> BUCKET(_["DEPT"]) .> MAP(BUCKET("entity", COUNT(_), "latest", TOP_BY(_, _["QTY"], "DESC", 1)))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:52
===

### name: plan.pure-memory.pipeline-past-the-depth-limit
--- note
250 pipe steps: stage 1 refuses a program past the depth limit, so the plan is pure_memory and never an exception (a host once raised RangeError at 20000).
